# 🎨 Visual Quick Reference - Environment Variables

## Command Decision Tree

```
┌─ START: What do you want to do?
│
├─ "I want to SEE the browser"
│  └─→ npm run test:headed
│
├─ "I want tests to run FAST"
│  └─→ npm run test:parallel
│
├─ "I want to run @smoke tests only"
│  ├─→ npm run test:tags (basic)
│  ├─→ CUCUMBER_TAGS="@critical" npm test (custom)
│  └─→ CUCUMBER_TAGS="@smoke and @critical" npm test (complex)
│
├─ "I want MAXIMUM speed (CI/CD)"
│  └─→ npm run test:parallel
│
├─ "I want to DEBUG an issue"
│  ├─→ npm run test:headed (see browser)
│  ├─→ HEADED=true CUCUMBER_TAGS="@specific" npm test (debug specific)
│  └─→ HEADED=true CUCUMBER_WORKERS=0 npm test (debug step by step)
│
└─ "I want ALL options combined"
   └─→ HEADED=true CUCUMBER_TAGS="@tag" CUCUMBER_WORKERS=4 npm test
```

