## Real-World Scenarios

### Scenario 1: Local Development - Debugging
```
HEADED=true CUCUMBER_WORKERS=0
Command: npm run test:headed
Result: Browser visible, one test at a time (easiest to debug)
```

### Scenario 2: Local Development - Fast
```
HEADED=false CUCUMBER_WORKERS=4
Command: npm run test:parallel
Result: Browser hidden, 4 tests running (fast testing)
```

### Scenario 3: Specific Test Suite
```
HEADED=false CUCUMBER_TAGS="@critical" CUCUMBER_WORKERS=0
Command: CUCUMBER_TAGS="@critical" npm test
Result: Only @critical tests, one at a time
```

### Scenario 4: CI/CD Pipeline
```
HEADED=false CUCUMBER_WORKERS=4
Command: npm run test:parallel
Result: Fast, parallel, automated (best for pipelines)
```

### Scenario 5: Production Smoke Test
```
HEADED=false CUCUMBER_TAGS="@smoke and @critical" CUCUMBER_WORKERS=4
Command: CUCUMBER_TAGS="@smoke and @critical" npm run test:parallel
Result: Fast validation of critical smoke tests
```

